WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.030
 Welcome Angelina Jolie.

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:01.830
 Hey

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.630
 Hello.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.970
You play Thena.
- I do.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.770
 Yes.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.820
We will talk to you both.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.960
So you both--

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.770
 I can't talk to her

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.790
 Are you leaving us now?

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.634
 No, I mean if you want me
to stay, I'll stay, but--

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:11.610
[LAUGHING]
- Talk to her.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.427
Here, let's please swap
places, at the very least.

00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:15.660
 No, it's like boy,
girl, boy, girl.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.070
 OK, all right.
Boy, girl, boy, girl.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:17.520
 All right

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.380
 So I have a question for
you, which actually both of you

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:19.910
can answer.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.077
Something that you
have beautifully

00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:24.030
talked about in interviews,
is having your heart

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.950
be a part of the
projects that you do,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.010
and how that's important.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.430
So how did you connect to Thena?

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.240
What did you find there?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.830
And for you what did you
find in Kingo that you

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.747
personally connected with?

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:34.980
 I think mine is
going to be easier.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.980
[LAUGHS] I was thinking
like, his insanity, for you.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.780
[LAUGHING]

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.090
 He's like Kingo is so big, and
you're actually quite humble.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.134
So I actually think you.

00:00:46.134 --> 00:00:49.470
 You know, for me, I
was, yeah I just sort

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:50.790
of took parts of myself.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:54.840
And took away any sort of worry.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.390
He's a guy who's
really unworried.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.490
I think being Kingo is
pretty easy, it's pretty fun.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.590
What was it?
- I love Kingo.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.240
 I have, you know
I've wanted to talk

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.110
to you about Thena for a long
time after watching the movie.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.667
Seeing you create
the character there,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.600
I've become the interviewer.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.500
 I know, It was like, all
right, like take over the mic.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.710
 It's so, it's, why
don't you talk about that?

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.170
Because I want to hear it?

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.170
 So did you, I thought I
was trying to avoid mine.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.090
 Oh you want to avoid it?

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.730
 We're not going to let
you out of the answer.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.970
 Well, she's, my
heart, it's a hard one.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:30.130
She's, she has, this
is the first time

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:30.930
I've talked about it.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.760
She has post-traumatic
stress disorder,

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.360
she's a little uneven.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.320
And I think she's
struggling with a lot

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.770
and she's not sure she can
be what she needs to be.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.150
She's not sure
she's strong enough,

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.480
she's not sure she can
still defend her family.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.427
 Well for both of
you, I'm curious.

00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:49.260
You know, you both have played
so many different parts.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.110
And you've had so many
superheroes, or like you know,

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.820
strong characters
that you played.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.620
Is there anything
that really connected

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.377
with you about your
character, that you

00:01:57.377 --> 00:01:58.410
really connected with the most?

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.720
Or that you learned about
yourself in playing this role?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.669
 I guess it's that
fragility, that it's OK to be

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:12.420
both fragile and also strong.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.040
It can go, it can
be the same person.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.270
 I really, you know, saw
that watching Angie work.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.390
Because you know, I'm a very
verbal person, the characters

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.190
that play are very verbal.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.470
And the character
that she created,

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.590
she conveys through her
physicality so well.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.250
It really was inspiring and
intimidating for me to watch.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.170
You really created
this person who

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:41.260
says so much without really
having to use their words,

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.060
you know.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.880
It really, it was
really special to watch.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.490
And then to see it come
together on screen,

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.200
she's so good in the movie.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.370
 Can you tell we
both are obsessed

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.270
with each other characters?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.570
[LAUGHING]

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.820
 So we're hoping
in the sequel, we

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.400
actually think our characters
are very good like,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.840
sparring partners.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:58.790
 I think so.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.580
 Because we're almost
polar opposites.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.380
 That's right.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.580
 But yet, they're both a
little like, out there, so.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.380
 That's right.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.250
I think we would make a--

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.050
 They'd be a good time.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:06.930
 Yeah, great pairing.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.100
That's exactly right.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.440
 I hope that Kevin Feige is
listening to this right now.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.510
Because you both have
some very good ideas.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.310
 Thank you.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.670
There you go, Kevin.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.650
 Well that's what
happens when you have

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.120
an Academy Award-nominated
screenwriter

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.410
and Academy Award winner.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.060
You're both such
wonderful artists.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.610
My last question is, you
know as full artists,

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:26.460
for you with the script, and the
writing, and the way the story

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:27.420
came together.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.720
What did you most appreciate
about that and the themes

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.190
that it has?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.660
 Family.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.680
We're a family.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:41.100
And it's and it's been too
long coming, this family.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.440
 Yeah, I think
that's exactly right.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.430
And we're a global family, you
know, we look like the world.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.140
For so long, we've
seen superheroes

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.380
that have looked like a small
percentage of the world.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.640
This superhero team
looks like the world.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.640
And I also, you know in
the last year and a half,

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.020
we've sort of learned that
we are on the same Earth.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.390
And we all share
the same problems,

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.610
like these boundaries and
stuff, they're not as important.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.310
These borders are not
as important as what

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.360
we really have in common.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.390
And this movie
really gets to that.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.160
It really gets to
the truth of the fact

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.620
that we're all on
this rock together,

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.420
and we have to take
care of each other.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.550
 That is a wonderful way
to end this interview.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.920
Thank you both so
much for stopping

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.710
by, talking live to the fans.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:24.510
We appreciate it.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.530
Have a wonderful time tonight.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.700
 Thank you, thanks for coming.

